      "flags": {},
      "order": 4,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "widgets_values": [
        "WINDOWED LONG-FORM \u2014 one latent, one denoising pass\n\nWhy this instead of chaining clips:\n  A chain hands each link to the next, and every measured chain fails\n  the same three ways \u2014 contrast climbs (+0.028 by link 4), identity\n  drifts, and the model reproduces the handed-over prefix then makes a\n  fresh decision at the seam (wave 15, never solved).\n\n  Windowing has no handoff. ONE latent is denoised once; windows only\n  bound the attention cost. So none of those three apply.\n\nREQUIRES A PATCHED COMFYUI. Read H3 Enable Context Windows' info: if it\nsays CANNOT USE THEM, this graph will not work \u2014 use H3 10 (chunking)\ninstead, which needs no patch.\n\nIt bounds attention, NOT memory: the whole latent stays on the GPU.\nIf a length will not fit, chunk it instead.\n\nEvery window sits at the clip ORIGIN. Continuity across a seam comes\nonly from overlap. Raise overlap_frames if seams show."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
